{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a91e5d32-20c8-47a3-b461-80a98f7e2d91",
    "name": "Auth Service API",
    "description": "Comprehensive Postman Test Collection for the Auth Service (Port 8081).\n\n### Features Covered:\n- **01 - Authentication**: Admin Login, User Registration (communicates with `address-service` on port 8082 to enrich UK geocoding coordinates), User Login, Token Refresh, Forgot Password, Reset Password, User Logout\n- **02 - Current User Profile**: Fetch (`/me`) and update current authenticated user profile with UK address\n- **03 - User Administration (RBAC)**: Paginated user list, user retrieval by ID, role assignment (`ROLE_ADMIN`), user deletion\n- **04 - Negative & Security Scenarios**: Bad credentials (401), duplicate registration conflict (400), non-admin access to admin routes (403), unauthenticated access (401), invalid postcode regex format validation (400)\n- **05 - Actuator & OpenAPI**: System health checks and OpenAPI 3.0 documentation specs\n\n### Variable Chaining & Automation:\n- Running `1.1 Admin Login` automatically captures `adminAccessToken`, `adminRefreshToken`, and `adminUserId`.\n- Running `1.2 Register New User` automatically creates a unique test user and stores `userAccessToken`, `userRefreshToken`, and `testUserId`.\n- Running `1.5 Forgot Password` automatically captures the generated `resetToken` for `1.6 Reset Password`.\n- All test scripts automatically update both Collection and Environment variables for seamless execution.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
